WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:04.540
Cut a mouse nerve.

2
00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:08.700
The part of each axon beyond the cut looks normal for about 36 hours.

3
00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:10.280
Then it falls to pieces.

4
00:00:11.080 --> 00:00:15.660
In one strain of mouse, the same cut axons stay intact for two weeks or more.

5
00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:17.780
What is different about that mouse?

6
00:00:18.633 --> 00:00:22.073
The axon is the long process that carries a neuron's output.

7
00:00:22.633 --> 00:00:24.473
The cell body holds the nucleus.

8
00:00:25.153 --> 00:00:29.493
People long assumed a cut stump simply starves, like a severed branch.

9
00:00:29.953 --> 00:00:36.133
But mice that lack one gene, called Sarm1, keep cut axons intact for a long time.

10
00:00:36.693 --> 00:00:40.233
If one mutation can stop the breakdown, something is running it.

11
00:00:40.817 --> 00:00:42.377
Here is how the program starts.

12
00:00:42.957 --> 00:00:48.717
An enzyme called NMNA -T2 works in the axon, and it is short -loved.

13
00:00:49.277 --> 00:00:53.897
The cell body must keep sending it down the axon, like trucks refilling a tank.

14
00:00:54.517 --> 00:00:55.797
A cut closes the road.

15
00:00:56.217 --> 00:01:00.857
The supply stops, and NMNA -T2 in the stump runs low.

16
00:01:01.867 --> 00:01:07.427
With NMNA -T2 gone, its raw material, NMN, builds up.

17
00:01:07.827 --> 00:01:10.207
And NAD+ +, begins to fall.

18
00:01:10.807 --> 00:01:15.467
NMNA -T enzymes make NAD+ +, from NMN.

19
00:01:15.907 --> 00:01:19.567
A protein called SARM1 waits in the axon, held shut.

20
00:01:20.067 --> 00:01:25.147
In the leading model, a rise in NMN, relative to NAD+, +, switches it on.

21
00:01:25.867 --> 00:01:27.567
SARM -1 is an enzyme.

22
00:01:28.087 --> 00:01:30.827
Once switched on, it cleaves NAD+.

23
00:01:30.827 --> 00:01:37.247
Then ATP falls. As energy fails, calcium rises inside the axon.

24
00:01:37.807 --> 00:01:41.707
Calcium switches on calpains, enzymes that cut proteins.

25
00:01:42.247 --> 00:01:45.767
The calpains cut the cytoskeleton, and the axon fragments.

26
00:01:46.407 --> 00:01:48.907
All of this happens in a stump with no nucleus.

27
00:01:49.767 --> 00:01:51.327
Now the slow mouse makes sense.

28
00:01:51.887 --> 00:01:57.127
Its Wlds protein is a longer -lived source of NMNAT activity.

29
00:01:57.687 --> 00:01:59.687
It keeps the tank full after the trucks stop.

30
00:02:00.227 --> 00:02:03.727
deletes arm one instead, and cut axons survive too.

31
00:02:04.327 --> 00:02:05.627
The stump is not just starving.

32
00:02:06.147 --> 00:02:09.447
It is running a program, and a program has parts that can be stopped.
